-- Migration 1917 — withdraw 156 stance chairs from the absence tier-B TOP BAND.
--
-- WHAT THIS IS. Tier B of the absence detector is the tier where the row states its own absence of
-- evidence AND carries something else beside it — a quotation, a named instrument, or an explicit
-- rung contrast. It is therefore the lower-yield tier, and at 813 actionable rows it was too large
-- to read blind. On 2026-10-09 the 307 hand-read tier-A rows were used as LABELS to fit a ranking
-- model (5-fold out-of-fold AUC 0.763), tier B was re-ranked, and the ranking was measured on two
-- blind samples before anything was read in bulk.
--
-- 🔑 THE MEASURED NUMBERS THIS FILE RESTS ON, none of them inherited:
--   * tier B's base rate is 43% (13/30 fresh uniform rows read under STANDARD.md, 95% CI 27-61%).
--     The previously remembered ~33% came from SIX rows and is withdrawn.
--   * the top band (score >= 0.80, 193 rows) was predicted at 80%. All 193 were then read by hand
--     and came in at 156/193 = 80.8%. The prediction and the result agree to within one row.
--
-- ⚖ ADJUDICATED UNDER A WRITTEN STANDARD, AND THE STANDARD WAS TESTED. C:/ev-stance-work/absence/
-- STANDARD.md was derived from the 101 KEEP rulings in the tier-A ledger rather than written from
-- opinion, because a blind re-read of 24 already-adjudicated rows had agreed only 17/24 — every
-- miss on the KEEP side. After the standard was written, a SECOND calibration on 24 FRESH rows
-- agreed 22/24 (92%), with 0 false KEEPs. Both residual misses have identified causes.
-- 🔴 A reader converging on ever LARGER numbers is converging on their own drift, exactly as a
-- detector converging on ever smaller numbers converges on its own bugs (#954).
--
-- ⚖ WHAT A BLANK HERE ASSERTS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT. It asserts that the row's own reasoning does
-- not support the chair it carries. It does NOT assert the person holds no view. Each row records
-- WHICH KIND of nothing it is, in its own INTERNAL RECORD prose.
--
-- 🔑 WHY A SEASON 2 BLANK AND NOT A SEASON 1 EDIT. Season 1 is closed and immutable. A Season 2
-- answer of 0 SUPPRESSES the pair — `NULLIF(pa.value, 0)`, with the guard deliberately OUTSIDE the
-- season collapse, so a blank in the newest season withdraws the answer rather than falling through
-- to the previous season's rung. Same mechanism as migrations 1914, 1915 and 1916.
--
-- COMPOSITION. 156 rows across 128 people. 143 are Season 1 pairs with no Season 2 answer, so
-- they INSERT. 13 are Season 2 rows where the defective answer IS the Season 2 answer, so they
-- UPDATE. One statement does both: (politician_id, topic_id, season_id) is the PK on BOTH tables.
--
-- THE SHAPES, counted over the 156 rows (the full per-row ledger is band193_calls.json, and the
-- reason code is written into each row's own INTERNAL RECORD prose):
--   NONCOSP 35 · OFFAXIS 25 · ADMITS 22 · RUNGTEXT 19 · AFFIRM 17 · AFFIL 11 · BODY 11 · AWAY 7 ·
--   SCORE 3 · DUTY 3 · COUNTERFACTUAL 3
-- 🔴 The largest single shape is NEW and tier-B specific: 35 rows whose entire evidence is a
-- NON-CO-SPONSORSHIP ("did not co-sponsor the Safe Communities Act"), 35 of which seat the
-- status-quo middle rung. Declining to sign a bill is not a position. It reached tier B rather than
-- tier A because naming the bill satisfied the instrument test.
--
-- ⚠ NOT BLANKED, deliberately — 37 of the 193. Rows where real, attributed, on-axis evidence sets
-- the direction and the absence only declines a neighbour that would require MORE (Barr's weighed
-- cosponsorships, Roeder's two named Maine roll calls, Boerner's three dated coverage votes); the
-- Northcut shape, where the omission is INSIDE the person's own document and the rung is about
-- emphasis (Ohlsen's and Ayala's road-only transportation pages); and defensive records, which ARE
-- the maintain rung.
--
-- ⚠ LEFT OPEN. T145 (Goodenough, taxes) is sound but VINTAGE — a 2008 recorded position held over
-- by "no 2026 statement found". It is NOT an absence defect and is not touched here. It belongs in
-- the re-research queue, where migration 1916 found 6 of 8 such rows failed.
--
-- ⚠ NOT A STANCE DEFECT, recorded here because it was found here: two DISTINCT politician rows are
-- both named "Jim Priest" (0bba9f72-… and 91dcb66a-…) and carry near-identical school-vouchers
-- reasoning. Both are blanked below on their own merits. The duplicate PERSON is a separate repair.
--
-- Applied by hand via psql; no migration runner exists in this repo, so "applied" means its data
-- effects are live. Guards below fail the whole transaction rather than write a partial result.

CREATE TEMP TABLE mig1917_decisions (
  politician_id     uuid   NOT NULL,
  topic_id          uuid   NOT NULL,
  topic_revision_id uuid   NOT NULL,
  reasoning         text   NOT NULL,
  ledger_no         text   NOT NULL
) ON COMMIT DROP;

